flowchart TD
    A[Prod region input] --> Q1{Input type?}
    Q1 -->|"Specific region — DEFAULT<br/>(PLC-001, Scenario 2)"| S1{Region<br/>classification?}
    Q1 -->|"Geography supplied — EXCEPTIONAL<br/>(PLC-002, Scenario 1)<br/>requires exception approval<br/>+ customer acknowledgement"| G1[Derive Prod = argmax PS_Prod<br/>over Standard regions in geography]
    G1 --> G2{Geography<br/>exhausted?}
    G2 -->|Yes| R1[Reject — never cross-geo<br/>or use Restricted region]
    G2 -->|No| ANCHOR[Validated Prod anchor]
    S1 -->|Standard| V1[Validate HC-1..HC-10] --> ANCHOR
    S1 -->|Restricted| EC[Exception Deployment Workflow]
    EC --> EC1{EC-1..EC-4 all met?<br/>explicit + Prod-only +<br/>approval + Scenario 2}
    EC1 -->|No| R2[Reject at first failing gate]
    EC1 -->|Yes| ANCHOR2[Exception Prod Anchor<br/>+ persisted approval ID<br/>+ capacity warning]
    ANCHOR --> NEXT[CVAL and DR selected<br/>sequentially from anchor]
    ANCHOR2 --> NEXT

    NOTE["Input-mode policy:<br/>• Specific exact region is the DEFAULT input (PLC-001) — ACRME validates it.<br/>• Geography-only selection is EXCEPTIONAL (PLC-002) — requires explicit exception<br/>approval + customer acknowledgement that the derived Prod region becomes the<br/>fixed seed until an approved migration changes it."]
